    "note": "The frigates a player can fly, first the starting one. The scene builder (CarrierBuilder.Frigates) makes a prefab of each and the start menu's roster from them. The starting frigate's guns are ball mounts on its gun pods (frigate_hardpoints.json); the others' are the turrets modelled on them, cut out by Tools/Blender/convert_frigates.py (frigate_<id>_hardpoints.json), which also gives where their CIWS mounts go. Every frigate has its turrets, at least one CIWS mount and one main gun (the bow beam). Speeds in m/s, turns in degrees a second; gunDamage is each shot's; beamDamage is a second's of the beam; cargo is the hold in tonnes (ore, refined materials and parts all count), slots how many ship parts (industry.json) it can have fitted, miningRate the mining laser's tonnes a second (8 if left out), and crew how many people work it (crew.json: short of 90% of them it works less well). The destroyers and the cruiser (category Destroyer or Cruiser, buildable) are built at a shipyard (industry.json ships) before they can be flown: they add ball-mounted guns at the hardpoints' mounts listed in mounts (by index), missiles (the magazine, fired from the hardpoints' launch cells and refilled when docked or landed at a site), and a destroyer has no main gun (noMainGun). A ship without a category is a Frigate. Rebuild (Tools > Carrier > Build Everything) after changing anything here.",
